        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: छागः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छागः (chāgaḥ) — \"a goat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छागः (chāgaḥ) is a goat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Like सिंहः (siṁhaḥ) and unlike वृकः (vṛkaḥ), it has no agreed cousin outside India: the goat words of Europe and this one do not line up. Two animals out of the same field, and only one of them carried its name across the family."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth holding on to, because it is what makes वृकः (vṛkaḥ) remarkable rather than ordinary. Ends in -अः."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three animals, and two different fates for a name."
            }
          ]
        },
