          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: वानरः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वानरः (vānaraḥ) — \"a monkey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वानरः (vānaraḥ) is a monkey."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words you own are sitting inside it: वनम्, the forest, and नरः, the man. Sanskrit's own commentators read वानरः (vānaraḥ) as the forest-man, and that reading has held for two thousand years, whatever later scholars have made of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the word costs you one new shape and pays back two old ones. Ends in -अः."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word built out of two you had already."
            }
          ]
        },
